<!--
=====================================================================================================
Trade DNA in R Markdown: the Streamlit pages "1 · Trade twins" and "5 · Luxembourg's partners",
rebuilt with plotly + crosstalk. No Shiny: everything interactive runs in the browser.

WHAT THE CODE NEEDS
  Packages ........ rmarkdown, dplyr, tidyr, plotly, crosstalk, htmltools, jsonlite   (install.packages(...))
                    (jsonlite comes with plotly)
  Two data files, both Eurostat Comext ds-045409, VALUE_IN_EUROS, annual:
    data/final_df.rds   Luxembourg as reporter x all partners x TOTAL + HS2 chapters x flows 1 and 2, 1999 on.
                        Columns PRODUCT_CODE, FLOW_CODE, PARTNER_CODE, TIME, VALUE_IN_EUROS (labels may stay;
                        PARTNER_LABEL is used to name partners the page does not know).
                        No reporter column needed: the file is Luxembourg.
    data/eu27_df.rds    the other 26 EU countries as reporters x partner WORLD x TOTAL + HS2 x flows 1 and 2,
                        same columns + REPORTER_CODE.  Made by:   Rscript r/fetch_eu27.R
                        (the CSV of the Python pipeline, data/raw/eu27_hs2.csv, is accepted too and used
                        automatically when the .rds is absent)
  The file paths in `params` are tried first; when one does not exist, the file is looked for relative to this
  .Rmd (which sits in r/ next to data/): ../data/<name>, data/<name>, <name>. A full path is written with
  forward slashes: "C:/Users/me/Documents/final_df.rds". The knit stops with the list of places tried otherwise.
  A file ending in .rds is read with readRDS(), anything else with read.csv(). Column names are matched
  case-insensitively (REPORTER_CODE/reporter, PARTNER_CODE/partner, PRODUCT_CODE/product, FLOW_CODE/flow,
  TIME/period, VALUE_IN_EUROS/value). Comext codes GR / GB are understood next to Eurostat's EL / UK.

HOW TO KNIT
  rmarkdown::render("r/trade_dna.Rmd")                                                # opens on exports, 2024
  rmarkdown::render("r/trade_dna.Rmd", params = list(flow = "1", year = "2019"))      # opens on imports, 2019
  rmarkdown::render("r/trade_dna.Rmd", params = list(data_lu = "C:/full/path/final_df.rds"))

IF eu27_df.rds IS MISSING the partners part still knits; the twins part shows a notice instead of charts.

WHAT IS INTERACTIVE (all in the browser, no server)
  A bar at the top of the page: Flow (imports / exports) and a Year slider. Every chart, number and
  sentence of the page follows them. The knit computes all flow x year combinations once and stores them
  in the HTML (a few MB); a small script swaps the data in the plotly charts when the controls move.
  Trade twins   : map, top 5, crosstalk selectize box for the trajectories, dropdown "Compare Luxembourg
                  with" (butterfly), heatmap, dropdown "Product" (product picker).
  Partners      : KPI tiles, dropdown "Product" (ranking), crosstalk selectize box (partners over time),
                  dropdown "Partner" (one partner in detail).

SAME NUMBERS AS THE PYTHON APP (tests/test_indicators.py):
  Finger-Kreinin FK(LU, c) = sum_i min(s_LU,i , s_c,i) on HS2 shares; product_overlap / collapse_overlap
  (butterfly), common_matrix (heatmap), product_twins (product picker); partner_table / partner_shares_over_time /
  partner_product_mix (partners page).
=====================================================================================================
-->

